  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Building back better post Covid-19. Enhancing skill development and job creation fot the youth in Angola</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The COVID-19 pandemic consitutes an unprecedented crisis with adverse sicioeconomic impacts in Angola. The negative shock on jobs and education has exacerbated multidimensional poverty and inequalities within the context of prolonged economic recession. RIsing unembplyment, informal work and school closure have hit the young Angolan population - eight out of ten Angolans will be under 35 yesars by 2021. This has led to tensions in densely-populated urban and peri-urban areas, which as resulted in social unrests.
The project aims at enhancing skills development to foster job opportunities for Angolan youth through the promotion of quality technical and vocational training (TVET), youth employment and entrepreneurship, and youth  engagement. Gender ratio in the project is 60% girls and 40 % boys.</narrative>
  </description>
